\itemize{
\item \code{dis_sorensen} (1 - C): Sorensen-type non-overlap;
\item \code{dis_jaccard} (1 - U): Jaccard-type non-overlap;
\item \code{dis_turnover_sorensen} (1 - V): Sorensen-type turnover;
\item \code{dis_turnover_jaccard} (1 - S): Jaccard-type turnover.
}

For q = 0 they reduce to the classic Sorensen and Jaccard family; for
q = 1 and 2 they generalise Horn and Morisita-Horn overlap.
